# The names a generated unit keeps across its groups' headers (defect 361,
# 2026-10-06): the list `runtime/heroes_guard_open.h` saves and
# `runtime/heroes_guard_close.h` gives back, held here so the unit can push
# again just before the close every one of them its program binds, which
# then keeps the header's meaning (`emit/macro_guard.hero`). Sorted by bytes,
# as many to a line as fit.
#
# It is three sets: every word `heroes_runtime.h` and `hero_os.h` write, a
# runtime macro's expansion included (`HERO_STR_LIT` writes `HeroStr` and the
# member `hero_body`); every name C11 gives the standard headers a unit reads,
# <stdbool.h> and <stddef.h> through the runtime before the groups and
# <stdint.h> and <math.h> after them (7.18, 7.19, 7.20, 7.12), but the macros
# of the last two the unit never writes (`LEFT`); and `main`. `macro_guard`'s
# tests hold the two runtime files to this list, every runtime word to it,
# the headers read before the groups to clang's two and the runtime's own,
# and every emitter module to the ten macros it may write, so a word, a
# header or a macro the compiler gains is a red test naming it.
#
# **The macros left out, since panel 205's R3 (defect 568)**: with `<stdint.h>`
# and `<math.h>` read after the groups, each of their macros is undefined
# when the guard saves it, so the guard gave back nothing whatever the
# headers defined, and a group's constant `#define MY_MAX INT32_MAX` lost
# `INT32_MAX` with the region, the library's include guard keeping it from
# coming back. A macro the unit's own C never writes needs no guard: its
# meaning after the groups is the headers' own business. The ones it writes
# are guarded and defined again (`runtime/heroes_standard.h`): four when the
# repair was measured, and ten since lane b18-guard met the round
# (2026-10-10), defect 567's division guard writing `INT8_MIN` and
# `INT8_C(-1)` at an `i8`'s width, and the same at `i16` and `i32`.

