# The functions of `<math.h>` (C11 7.12) the list holds, `fmod` among them
# since the unit's own C writes an `f64` `%` as `__builtin_fmod` (defect
# d-lane-macro-members2-1, 2026-11-25; `emit/operator.hero`), and as the
# runtime's `hero_f64_rem` since defect d-lane-macro-members4-2 the same day,
# which links with no maths library: a name the unit's own C never writes, which the guard keeps for the C library's `<math.h>` read
# after the groups (defect 568) and which `heroes_standard.h` now reads with
# each such name a bound macro reaches saved and undefined (defect 2059,
# `cli/bound_kept.hero`), so the guard can leave such a name as a group's
# header made it where a bound macro expands to it. `macro_guard`'s test holds
# every emitter module to writing none.
constant MATH_LINES: [str]
    [
        "acos acosf acosh acoshf acoshl acosl asin asinf asinh asinhf asinhl"
        "asinl atan atan2 atan2f atan2l atanf atanh atanhf atanhl atanl cbrt"
        "cbrtf cbrtl ceil ceilf ceill copysign copysignf copysignl cos cosf"
